###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_18ce5200_00f5_45bb_8c6f_6fb128cd41ae
ns1:EMMO_18ce5200_00f5_45bb_8c6f_6fb128cd41ae rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf ns1:EMMO_985bec21_989f_4b9e_a4b3_735d88099c3c ;
                                              rdfs:comment "A reference can be a measurement unit, a measurement procedure, a reference material, or a combination of such (VIM3 1.1 NOTE 2)."@en ;
                                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siunits#> ;
                                              rdfs:label "MetrologicalReference"@en ;
                                              skos:prefLabel "MetrologicalReference"@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db "EquivalentTo: StandardUnit or MeasurementUnit or ProcedureUnit" ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "A reference can be a measurement unit, a measurement procedure, a reference material, or a combination of such (VIM3 1.1 NOTE 2)."@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f """A symbolic is recognized as reference unit also if it is not part of a quantity (e.g. as in the sentence \"the Bq is the reference unit of Becquerel\").
For this reason we can't declare the axiom:
MetrologicalReference SubClassOf: inverse(hasMetrologicalReference) some Quantity
because there exist reference units without being part of a quantity.
This is peculiar to EMMO, where quantities as syntatic entities (explicit quantities) are distinct with quantities as semantic entities (properties)."""@en .


