###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_43a4e80d_6ae9_45ed_8cfb_fd0a5339bf87
ns1:EMMO_43a4e80d_6ae9_45ed_8cfb_fd0a5339bf87 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf ns1:EMMO_e7aac247_31d6_4b2e_9fd2_e842b1b7ccac ;
                                              owl:disjointWith ns1:EMMO_b295158f_fda4_4124_ab58_d9ea4ccfca5a ;
                                              rdfs:comment "A causal system that is the representation of a Feynman diagram, where quantum represents the real particles entering and exiting the system."@en ,
                                                           """A fundamental physical process is made of one or more standard particles as input, and one or more standard particles as output, where each input is direct cause of each output.
Each fundamental physical phenomena refers to a Feynman diagram, hence is made at least of three standard model particles.
This requirement implies that a physical phenomena is either a decay, annihilation, interaction, collapse or creation phenomena (fundamental) or a composition of them (non-fundamental)."""@en ;
                                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/reference/standardmodel#> ;
                                              rdfs:label "FundamentalPhysicalSystem"@en ;
                                              skos:prefLabel "FundamentalPhysicalSystem"@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13 """A fundamental physical process is made of one or more standard particles as input, and one or more standard particles as output, where each input is direct cause of each output.
Each fundamental physical phenomena refers to a Feynman diagram, hence is made at least of three standard model particles.
This requirement implies that a physical phenomena is either a decay, annihilation, interaction, collapse or creation phenomena (fundamental) or a composition of them (non-fundamental)."""@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db "DisjointUnionOf: Collapse, Interaction, Decay" ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "A causal system that is the representation of a Feynman diagram, where quantum represents the real particles entering and exiting the system."@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f "A fundamental system is expressed as a complete bipartite directed graph K(m,n) of quantums, m being the number of originating quantums, and n being the receiving quantums."@en .


