###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/chemical-substance#substance_180ac854_f837_46ed_a4d8_4407b91fb95a
:substance_180ac854_f837_46ed_a4d8_4407b91fb95a rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf :substance_dc68514f_b592_4e1b_a00f_fbb29f2fafbd ;
                                                rdfs:comment "A cationic polymer consisting of an arylene backbone functionalized with imidazolium groups, forming an ion-conducting polymeric material."@en ;
                                                rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
                                                rdfs:label "PolyAryleneImidazolium"@en ;
                                                skos:note "Poly(arylene imidazolium)s are a distinct class of cationic polymers featuring imidazolium-functionalized arylene backbones, widely used in ion-conducting membranes and electrochemical applications. They exhibit unique properties such as ionic conductivity, thermal stability, and tunable charge transport behavior. Including this term is necessary to clearly distinguish this polymer family within broader polymer and ionic liquid material ontologies."@en ,
                                                          "This polymer class is primarily used in advanced electrochemical systems such as fuel cell membranes and CO2 separation materials. The absence of standardized ontology entries motivates explicit inclusion for interoperability in materials informatics frameworks."@en ;
                                                skos:prefLabel "PolyAryleneImidazolium"@en ;
                                                ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "A cationic polymer consisting of an arylene backbone functionalized with imidazolium groups, forming an ion-conducting polymeric material."@en .


