###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/chemical-substance#substance_9f3b59a2_b2af_4b5b_919c_0c68d10f3edf
:substance_9f3b59a2_b2af_4b5b_919c_0c68d10f3edf rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf :substance_b325bdd7_0adf_4522_a4ef_20cd6929e094 ;
                                                rdfs:comment "A perfluoroalkyl substance consisting of a fully fluorinated carbon chain terminating in a carboxylic acid functional group."@en ;
                                                rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
                                                rdfs:label "PerfluorocarboxylicAcid"@en ;
                                                skos:note "Perfluorocarboxylic acids (PFCAs) are a distinct and widely recognized subclass of PFAS with a shared structural motif and consistent chemical behavior. They are frequently referenced in environmental science, toxicology, and regulatory frameworks as a separate category from other fluorinated substances. Including this term enables precise semantic classification and interoperability across chemical substance ontologies."@en ,
                                                          "Perfluorocarboxylic acids include compounds such as trifluoroacetic acid and perfluorooctanoic acid, which are relevant due to their persistence, bioaccumulation potential, and industrial use. The class is commonly treated"@en ;
                                                skos:prefLabel "PerfluorocarboxylicAcid"@en ;
                                                ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "A perfluoroalkyl substance consisting of a fully fluorinated carbon chain terminating in a carboxylic acid functional group."@en .


