###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/chemical-substance#substance_c1755292_fb2a_46a9_aeb1_84067b0a087c
:substance_c1755292_fb2a_46a9_aeb1_84067b0a087c rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf :substance_dc68514f_b592_4e1b_a00f_fbb29f2fafbd ;
                                                rdfs:comment "A cationic polymer consisting of an aryl backbone functionalized with piperidinium groups, used primarily in ion-conducting membrane materials."@en ;
                                                rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
                                                rdfs:label "PolyArylAmmonium"@en ;
                                                skos:note "Poly(aryl piperidinium)s are a class of cationic polymers featuring piperidinium-functionalized aryl backbones, commonly used in anion exchange membranes and electrochemical energy systems. They are structurally and functionally distinct from other ionic polymers such as imidazolium- or ammonium-based systems. Including this term enables precise semantic classification of emerging membrane materials in electrochemical and polymer ontologies."@en ,
                                                          "Poly(aryl piperidinium)s are an emerging class of anion exchange membrane materials used in alkaline fuel cells and related electrochemical devices. Their distinct backbone–cation architecture differentiates them from imidazolium- and ammonium-based polymer electrolytes, motivating explicit ontology representation for materials informatics and energy systems modeling."@en ;
                                                skos:prefLabel "PolyArylAmmonium"@en ;
                                                ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "A cationic polymer consisting of an aryl backbone functionalized with piperidinium groups, used primarily in ion-conducting membrane materials."@en .


